# Rust
/target/
/**/target/
# Per-crate cargo-bundle output (target/release/bundle/) — never the
# source icon directory under crates/*/assets/bundle/.
/**/target/**/bundle/
**/*.rs.bk

# mdbook user guide build artifacts
/book/build/

# Docs subsumed by the MDBook user guide (book/src/). Kept on disk for
# reference but not tracked in git.
#
# `docs/compatibility_matrix.json` is deliberately NOT listed here. The book
# chapter is the curated human summary, but the JSON is the authoritative
# machine-readable snapshot of `vortex-bevy support-matrix --format json`,
# and `cli_boundary.rs` asserts the checked-in file matches the typed CLI
# model. A test cannot `include_str!` an ignored path, so ignoring it broke
# every clean CI checkout. It is regenerated with
#   cargo run -q -p vortex-bevy -- support-matrix --format json > docs/compatibility_matrix.json
# and the release gate re-checks it.
/docs/operations_and_architecture_guide.md
/docs/performance_baseline.md
/docs/release_hardening.md
/docs/t29_streaming_bottleneck_analysis.md

# Auto-generated Wiggum scaffold artifacts. Regenerated by the scaffold
# on each task completion; not authored by hand.
/PROGRESS.md
/plan.toml
/features.json
/tasks/

# Local IDE / agent / tool state. Not part of the project; user-specific.
# Tests and build never read from these.
.coraline/
.vscode/
.claude/
/.mcp.json
/.config/dotnet-tools.json

